From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Inference-Bench Oracle <infb@example.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] oracle: optimize_glm_5_2_8xb200_mtp_open marker -- semantically neutral, non-empty

WHAT THIS IS. A no-op marker: it inserts two comment lines into vllm/__init__.py and changes
nothing at runtime. Two jobs, and it is deliberately the same asset for both.

  1. ORACLE ASSET. The oracle agent applies this file. Without a real patch the run returns
     reason=no_patch and reward 0.0, which proves nothing about the task -- it is the most
     common false zero in this benchmark.
  2. NOISE PROBE. Semantically neutral means the true speedup is 1.000 at every point, so a
     scored run of it measures this profile's NOISE FLOOR and nothing else. vllm/__init__.py is
     chosen over a new file precisely because it IS imported on every engine boot: a patch the
     engine never loads cannot control for whether the harness measured the candidate tree at
     all.

EXPECT reward ~= 0. A neutral patch earns max(0, geomean - 1) ~= 0 by construction. A reward
materially above 0 here is a measurement of noise, not of an optimization -- which is the point.

SCORED PROFILE at the time this was written: mtp_longctx_8k out=4096 scored=c1(n=2)/c8(n=16)/c32(n=64).

APPLIES AT both pins this patch targets: vllm/__init__.py is byte-identical at v0.20.1 and
v0.24.0 (3661 bytes both), and each context line below appears exactly once in each, so
`git apply --check` passes against the real file at either pin.
---
 vllm/__init__.py | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/vllm/__init__.py b/vllm/__init__.py
--- a/vllm/__init__.py
+++ b/vllm/__init__.py
@@ -4,6 +4,8 @@

 # The version.py should be independent library, and we always import the
 # version library first.  Such assumption is critical for some customization.
+# inference-bench optimize_glm_5_2_8xb200_mtp_open: oracle marker / neutral noise probe.
+#   No runtime effect. See solution/known_good.patch for why this file and not a new one.
 from .version import __version__, __version_tuple__  # isort:skip

 import typing
